*   Clearly, the Actual Expenses method will yield a much higher deduction, significantly lowering your taxable freelance profit.

### 3. Other Deductions (Above-the-Line)
These deductions lower your Adjusted Gross Income (AGI) before the standard deduction is applied:
*   **Student Loan Interest:** You paid $2,900, but the IRS caps this deduction at **$2,500**. Furthermore, because your Modified Adjusted Gross Income (MAGI) will be roughly $83,000, you fall into the 2023 phase-out range for single filers ($75,000 to $90,000). Your $2,500 maximum deduction will be partially reduced based on this phase-out.
*   **Self-Employment Tax Deduction:** You will owe self-employment tax (Medicare and Social Security) on your net freelance profit. You are allowed to deduct 50% of this tax amount as an adjustment to income.

